 # Bitcoin-Backed USDC One-Loan System Architecture
 
-Source brief: [Technical Brief](../../technical-brief.md)
+The [architecture guide](../guide/architecture.md) explains the system for readers. This record holds its exact purpose, binding, authority and boundaries.
 
-## System Overview
-
-The product coordinates one borrower, one selected lender, Bitcoin collateral, and USDC settlement on Base. Its five domains separate agreement meaning, participant Bitcoin authority, Base value movement, verified observation and conditional fallback, and durable application coordination. The separation matters because each can report progress without acquiring another's authority: login is not a Vault unlock, an accepted command is not a chain fact, and a Base refund is not a confirmed Bitcoin recovery.
-
-Loan Terms And Commitments supplies the shared identity and immutable candidate binding. Participant Access And Loan Operations presents and persists the workspace and sends narrowly bound actions to participant Vaults. Bitcoin Authorization And Recovery constructs and validates fixed participant-authorized packages, while Base USDC Settlement And Funding controls its own funding, acceptance, repayment, claim, and refund transitions. Base Observation And Fallback Review qualifies named Base events and independently constrains optional `S` publication. A normal repayment lets the lender disclose `Y`; lender silence can lead to a Base refund and, only for an activated precommitted fallback loan, conditional `S` recovery. Either Bitcoin path becomes final only when the expected spend confirms.
-
-Each domain below is a complete reading destination; responsibility and contract links provide precise detail. Runtime topology, construction dependencies, and state/sequence views are separate derived perspectives in the [visual index](../visuals/index.html). They do not replace this written architecture. Existing approval-wording and fee/count discrepancies identified by the migration remain unresolved source issues; this documentation revision does not choose new behavior.
+Source brief: [Technical Brief](../../technical-brief.md)
 
